1
00:00:00,977 --> 00:00:03,078
We...

2
00:00:03,078 --> 00:00:08,289
How long do we have to be pitiful like this
until it's okay to be happy?

3
00:00:08,289 --> 00:00:12,065
For pitiful people like us,
wouldn't it be better like this now?

4
00:00:12,065 --> 00:00:13,733
<i>Mitsuru probably...</i>

5
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:14,920
[3-4-4 Minamisensu]

6
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,576
[Minami-Shinshu, Nagano Prefecture]
<i>won't come back.</i>

7
00:00:21,781 --> 00:00:24,881
Hello, my name is Sakiko Seo.

8
00:00:24,881 --> 00:00:27,474
Is Mitsuru at home?

9
00:00:28,417 --> 00:00:29,517
Yes?

10
00:00:29,517 --> 00:00:34,033
Sorry to show up so suddenly like this.
You're Mr. Sonoda, right?

11
00:00:34,033 --> 00:00:35,085
Yes.

12
00:00:35,085 --> 00:00:38,801
Nice to meet you.
I work at a children's welfare institution.

13
00:00:38,801 --> 00:00:40,861
My surname is Hiraoka.

14
00:00:40,861 --> 00:00:44,901
Oh, was it you who
used to take care of Azusa?

15
00:00:44,901 --> 00:00:46,793
All right, please come in.

16
00:00:46,793 --> 00:00:50,597
I was extremely shocked and saddened by this.

17
00:00:50,597 --> 00:00:55,673
But I also knew that
she was married and had a child,

18
00:00:55,673 --> 00:00:58,034
and that made me happy.

19
00:00:58,693 --> 00:01:02,157
I'm very happy that
Azusa was able to meet someone

20
00:01:02,157 --> 00:01:05,794
whom she wanted to marry.

21
00:01:07,193 --> 00:01:10,581
Though it would be even better
if she was still with us.

22
00:01:10,581 --> 00:01:12,085
Yes.

23
00:01:12,085 --> 00:01:16,234
So today I've come to see her husband.

24
00:01:16,961 --> 00:01:19,021
Hey, don't do that.

25
00:01:19,753 --> 00:01:21,994
Oh, please feel free to have a seat.

26
00:01:33,285 --> 00:01:34,945
Now there's a familiar face from the past.

27
00:01:34,945 --> 00:01:37,594
- It's been a while.
- Thanks for stopping by.

28
00:01:40,149 --> 00:01:42,817
- Is this about Azusa?
- Yes.

29
00:01:42,817 --> 00:01:46,109
- I said hello to her husband.
- Ah, I see.

30
00:01:46,109 --> 00:01:48,477
Did you know?

31
00:01:48,477 --> 00:01:51,414
She was married and had a child.

32
00:01:51,414 --> 00:01:53,761
I was surprised. Azusa...

33
00:01:53,761 --> 00:01:55,493
Yes.

34
00:01:56,521 --> 00:01:58,514
About that child...

35
00:02:02,041 --> 00:02:04,474
Hello, Chizuru?

36
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:09,754
No luck, he wasn't there.

37
00:02:10,509 --> 00:02:13,754
And the person living there
didn't know anything about Mitsuru either.

38
00:02:14,709 --> 00:02:18,005
I wonder what that address was all about?

39
00:02:18,005 --> 00:02:19,909
No, no, I'm by myself.

40
00:02:20,825 --> 00:02:23,474
With that, I've done everything I can now.

41
00:02:24,857 --> 00:02:26,914
I'm going to give up.

42
00:02:31,121 --> 00:02:38,049
[Episode 5]

43
00:02:52,641 --> 00:02:54,191
[Cream Cheese]

44
00:02:54,191 --> 00:02:57,274
[Best before before opening: 2025/08/17]

45
00:03:10,113 --> 00:03:12,674
<i>It's been almost one year since the accident.</i>

46
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:19,314
<i>Mitsuru isn't coming back.</i>

47
00:03:26,309 --> 00:03:28,285
[Daikon 239 yen]

48
00:03:28,285 --> 00:03:30,573
- Sakiko!
- Sho, no running.

49
00:03:30,573 --> 00:03:32,721
- Ah, hello, Sho!
- Oh, sorry.

50
00:03:32,721 --> 00:03:35,073
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

51
00:03:35,073 --> 00:03:36,283
Do you know what you're having
for dinner tonight?

52
00:03:36,283 --> 00:03:37,365
Would you like to eat at my place?

53
00:03:37,365 --> 00:03:38,801
- Is that okay?
- Yes.

54
00:03:38,801 --> 00:03:40,393
I visited your place last week.

55
00:03:40,393 --> 00:03:42,321
All right, then next time
you're welcome at my place again.

56
00:03:42,321 --> 00:03:43,534
Okay, we can alternate.

57
00:03:43,534 --> 00:03:45,513
Oh sorry, let me take that for you.

58
00:03:45,513 --> 00:03:46,965
Thank you very much.

59
00:03:46,965 --> 00:03:50,881
Sho, we'll be having dinner
at Sakiko's tonight.

60
00:03:50,881 --> 00:03:53,261
- Yay!
- Yay!

61
00:03:53,261 --> 00:03:55,189
- The 50% off sale is about to start.
- Starting now...

62
00:03:55,189 --> 00:03:57,125
- 50% off, 50% off!
- All prepared foods, 50% off.

63
00:03:57,125 --> 00:03:58,969
Great, great!

64
00:03:58,969 --> 00:04:00,105
- What's there? What looks good?
- Which one do you want?

65
00:04:00,105 --> 00:04:01,997
- What looks good?
- Which one?

66
00:04:01,997 --> 00:04:05,154
Is it really okay to not tell Sakiko?

67
00:04:07,117 --> 00:04:10,649
Understand. If that's the case,
then there's even more reason for me to go.

68
00:04:10,649 --> 00:04:12,434
I'm worried, so...

69
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:17,034
Sunday, right? Please tell me the address.

70
00:04:18,765 --> 00:04:20,553
Okay.

71
00:04:22,549 --> 00:04:24,257
You know how there are some things

72
00:04:24,257 --> 00:04:27,497
that you don't ever get around to washing
unless you really decide to do it?

73
00:04:27,497 --> 00:04:30,637
- Like cushion covers, for example.
- Yes.

74
00:04:30,637 --> 00:04:33,854
Coming here on Saturdays
has become a regular part of my routine.

75
00:04:33,854 --> 00:04:37,054
If I were to take those covers off and
bring them with me every time I come here,

76
00:04:37,054 --> 00:04:40,685
I think I'd be able to
wash them properly once a week.

77
00:04:40,685 --> 00:04:43,737
They're being washed in there right now.

78
00:04:43,737 --> 00:04:45,893
I see. That could be a good thing.

79
00:04:45,893 --> 00:04:48,654
So do you really wash
cushion covers once a week?

80
00:04:48,654 --> 00:04:51,093
Well, I do in the summer.

81
00:04:51,093 --> 00:04:54,419
Oh dear, I don't wash mine even once a month.

82
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:58,054
What about your curtains?
How often do you wash those?

83
00:04:58,054 --> 00:05:01,769
Curtains? No, I don't have
any memory of washing those.

84
00:05:01,769 --> 00:05:03,285
I can understand that.

85
00:05:03,285 --> 00:05:05,073
What is it?

86
00:05:08,625 --> 00:05:12,597
Sho has an overnight stay
at his nursery school coming up.

87
00:05:12,597 --> 00:05:14,605
For one night next Thursday.

88
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:18,025
I see. The parents seem
more nervous about it than the kids.

89
00:05:18,025 --> 00:05:20,353
It'll be the first night I've spent
on my own for quite some time.

90
00:05:20,353 --> 00:05:22,221
Ah, I suppose that's true.

91
00:05:22,221 --> 00:05:24,973
I'm always alone, though.

92
00:05:24,973 --> 00:05:27,549
But it's not so bad once you get used to it.

93
00:05:27,549 --> 00:05:29,785
There's something about your job, right?

94
00:05:29,785 --> 00:05:31,901
You're very busy on the third Friday
of the month, right?

95
00:05:31,901 --> 00:05:34,985
- Yes.
- So Thursdays aren't that busy?

96
00:05:35,633 --> 00:05:37,341
Are you usually free in the evenings?

97
00:05:37,341 --> 00:05:40,234
- You mean Thursday evenings?
- Yes.

98
00:05:48,445 --> 00:05:51,074
I suppose I'm busy.

99
00:05:51,757 --> 00:05:52,889
Sorry.

100
00:05:52,889 --> 00:05:56,285
No, no, there's no need to apologize.
Huh? Why are you apologizing?

101
00:05:56,285 --> 00:05:58,514
All I asked was
if you were free on Thursdays.

102
00:06:00,517 --> 00:06:01,673
Right, right. Sorry.

103
00:06:01,673 --> 00:06:03,574
It's fine, really.

104
00:06:03,574 --> 00:06:06,854
It's just that I've heard about
how busy your work is.

105
00:06:06,854 --> 00:06:10,014
- Yes, exactly. Oh, sorry.
- No no, it's fine.

106
00:06:10,014 --> 00:06:12,294
Ah, let me go get some small change.

107
00:06:12,294 --> 00:06:17,365
Let's see, I can only use
1,000 yen bills here.

108
00:06:17,365 --> 00:06:19,897
And it looks like
I happen to have that here...

109
00:06:19,897 --> 00:06:22,997
I promised my teacher
I'd go swimming tomorrow too.

110
00:06:22,997 --> 00:06:26,641
Oh, but tomorrow won't work.
I'll be taking you for a drive.

111
00:06:26,641 --> 00:06:29,354
But we're just going there
to leave some flowers, right?

112
00:06:31,609 --> 00:06:33,613
That's not all.

113
00:06:33,613 --> 00:06:36,274
What really matters is how you feel about it.

114
00:06:36,989 --> 00:06:39,645
If Mom's there, then I want to go.

115
00:06:39,645 --> 00:06:41,577
But she isn't, right?

116
00:07:08,494 --> 00:07:10,309
- Huh?
- Huh?

117
00:07:16,574 --> 00:07:18,389
- Hey, hello.
- Goodbye.

118
00:07:18,389 --> 00:07:20,957
Hey, wait. Hold on a second.

119
00:07:20,957 --> 00:07:23,009
What is it?

120
00:07:23,009 --> 00:07:25,034
What do you mean, "what is it"?

121
00:07:26,329 --> 00:07:28,841
It's been almost a year now.

122
00:07:28,841 --> 00:07:33,578
Is that all? Then why are you
all dressed up like that?

123
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,593
This is for... something else.

124
00:07:35,593 --> 00:07:37,753
Then what about the shop?

125
00:07:37,753 --> 00:07:40,481
- I closed it.
- Just for coming all the way here?

126
00:07:40,481 --> 00:07:42,313
Yes. There's also something else
I need to take care of.

127
00:07:44,433 --> 00:07:46,281
I see.

128
00:07:47,641 --> 00:07:50,049
It's quite humid today.

129
00:07:50,049 --> 00:07:52,594
Yes, it sure is.

130
00:07:54,297 --> 00:07:57,014
- All right, then I'll be on my way now.
- Okay.

131
00:07:57,014 --> 00:08:01,221
Oh right, isn't there supposed to be
a good soba restaurant around here?

132
00:08:01,221 --> 00:08:04,625
Yes, there is. Want to go together?

133
00:08:04,625 --> 00:08:06,481
I came here by car.

134
00:08:18,965 --> 00:08:22,713
[Temporarily closed]

135
00:08:34,505 --> 00:08:39,085
That other matter you said you had to
take care of, is it a funeral or something?

136
00:08:39,085 --> 00:08:40,753
Yes.

137
00:08:40,753 --> 00:08:42,874
Whose funeral do you think it is?

138
00:08:44,317 --> 00:08:47,874
Well, I wouldn't know that...

139
00:08:50,345 --> 00:08:52,633
Huh?

140
00:08:52,633 --> 00:08:54,473
What is it?

141
00:08:55,173 --> 00:08:57,234
It's not Mr. Seo's.

142
00:08:58,233 --> 00:08:59,833
That was a shame.

143
00:09:03,369 --> 00:09:06,834
Anyway, why were you there
leaving flowers for Azusa?

144
00:09:11,053 --> 00:09:13,533
Please excuse me for a moment.

145
00:09:13,533 --> 00:09:17,794
Hello, Sakiko? What's the matter?

146
00:09:19,149 --> 00:09:22,154
Yes, that's right. Something urgent came up.

147
00:09:23,245 --> 00:09:24,993
Is something the matter?

148
00:09:25,777 --> 00:09:28,733
Ah, yes, that's right.

149
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:31,913
I'm sorry, I should have
contacted you before.

150
00:09:33,385 --> 00:09:37,314
Oh, no problem. All right then,
talk to you later.

151
00:09:39,265 --> 00:09:41,277
That was Sakiko.

152
00:09:41,277 --> 00:09:44,361
Sounds like she went to
help out with the shop.

153
00:09:44,361 --> 00:09:46,274
I hadn't heard anything about that.

154
00:09:50,617 --> 00:09:53,034
Anyway, what were we just talking about?

155
00:09:54,665 --> 00:09:57,914
Why did you come all the way out here
just to leave flowers for Azusa?

156
00:09:58,685 --> 00:10:04,074
Well, I just came all the way out here
to leave a flower in respect, that's all.

157
00:10:04,693 --> 00:10:08,754
And I haven't been able to
do anything for Azusa this past year.

158
00:10:11,709 --> 00:10:14,261
I've been curious about this for a while now.

159
00:10:14,261 --> 00:10:15,472
When you mentioned my wife,

160
00:10:15,472 --> 00:10:18,569
you said that she was
a pretty and younger woman, right?

161
00:10:18,569 --> 00:10:23,565
Her name... and maybe you even
went so far as to ask about her age.

162
00:10:23,565 --> 00:10:26,537
But a pretty and younger woman,
or something like that...

163
00:10:26,537 --> 00:10:30,034
I've been wondering if Mitsuru would really
talk about someone's appearances like that.

164
00:10:31,413 --> 00:10:33,277
Mr. Seo...

165
00:10:33,881 --> 00:10:37,101
You don't really know anything
about Mitsuru Seo, do you?

166
00:10:37,101 --> 00:10:39,994
Well, I've never met him before,
but I think I have a pretty good idea.

167
00:10:40,685 --> 00:10:44,314
Because I've heard a lot about him
from someone who does know him well.

168
00:10:47,653 --> 00:10:49,417
I see.

169
00:10:52,621 --> 00:10:55,434
Did you ever meet Azusa before?

170
00:10:58,565 --> 00:11:01,205
Yes, she visited the shop.

171
00:11:01,205 --> 00:11:02,489
What for?

172
00:11:02,489 --> 00:11:04,894
Well, it is a coffee shop,
so she came to get some coffee, of course.

173
00:11:04,894 --> 00:11:09,773
No, what I mean is, do you ask
each customer for their name

174
00:11:09,773 --> 00:11:12,394
and their relationship with the shop manager?

175
00:11:15,805 --> 00:11:17,748
Well, the day that Azusa came by the shop,

176
00:11:17,748 --> 00:11:19,981
Mr. Seo happened to not be working that day.

177
00:11:19,981 --> 00:11:22,229
She asked me if Mr. Mitsuru Seo was there.

178
00:11:22,229 --> 00:11:25,393
When I told her that he wasn't working
that day, she seemed disappointed.

179
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:28,417
I was curious,
so I asked about their relationship.

180
00:11:28,417 --> 00:11:31,185
And then she said that
on the third Friday of every month,

181
00:11:31,185 --> 00:11:33,805
they chatted at the laundromat.

182
00:11:33,805 --> 00:11:35,917
She heard that he worked at the coffee shop,

183
00:11:35,917 --> 00:11:38,354
so she wanted to surprise him by stopping by.

184
00:11:39,277 --> 00:11:42,149
That's all I heard.

185
00:11:42,149 --> 00:11:44,817
When I asked her if there was anything
she wanted me to pass on to Mr. Seo,

186
00:11:44,817 --> 00:11:47,345
she said no, it was fine.

187
00:11:47,345 --> 00:11:51,314
And she also told me not to tell Mr. Seo
that she'd stopped by.

188
00:11:52,165 --> 00:11:53,585
That's not like her.

189
00:11:53,585 --> 00:11:55,801
Well, I only met her once.

190
00:11:55,801 --> 00:11:58,434
You can't expect me to give
a really high-quality imitation.

191
00:12:05,637 --> 00:12:08,634
Thanks for the food. I'm headed this way.

192
00:12:09,305 --> 00:12:10,629
Hey.

193
00:12:10,629 --> 00:12:12,717
Yes?

194
00:12:12,717 --> 00:12:15,354
You've been in contact with Mitsuru, right?

195
00:12:17,861 --> 00:12:21,314
Does he have any intention of coming back?

196
00:12:22,865 --> 00:12:26,669
If so, would something change
for you as a result, Mr. Sonoda?

197
00:12:26,669 --> 00:12:28,441
For example, feelings?

198
00:12:36,193 --> 00:12:40,665
Anyway, I don't see any reason
why you couldn't get closer to Sakiko.

199
00:12:41,457 --> 00:12:44,994
It's not like you'd be
causing trouble for anyone.

200
00:12:47,401 --> 00:12:49,297
See you later.

201
00:12:51,929 --> 00:12:55,314
The sewing machine... the sewing machine...

202
00:13:20,561 --> 00:13:22,493
Stepladder...

203
00:13:22,493 --> 00:13:26,293
[Stepladder]

204
00:13:30,261 --> 00:13:33,677
Whatever, I'm going to the home improvement
store anyway, so I suppose it's fine.

205
00:13:33,677 --> 00:13:36,074
Huh? What is it?

206
00:13:38,153 --> 00:13:40,441
I've been thinking of
breaking up with my wife.

207
00:13:40,441 --> 00:13:44,277
Huh? Really?

208
00:13:44,277 --> 00:13:46,057
Yes.

209
00:13:46,849 --> 00:13:50,229
Have you really given it some thought?
Are you sure that's okay?

210
00:13:50,229 --> 00:13:52,794
Yes, I've made my decision.

211
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:56,857
I see. Got it.

212
00:13:56,857 --> 00:13:58,925
Yes.

213
00:14:01,765 --> 00:14:04,634
All right, then I think
we should break up as well.

214
00:14:05,945 --> 00:14:07,761
No, I didn't say I was breaking up
with you, Chizuru.

215
00:14:07,761 --> 00:14:12,049
I don't want to cause trouble for others.

216
00:14:12,049 --> 00:14:13,449
Huh?

217
00:14:13,449 --> 00:14:16,025
When I found out that
you were married, Takuma,

218
00:14:16,025 --> 00:14:18,597
I thought about breaking up with you
just because of that.

219
00:14:18,597 --> 00:14:21,584
I thought I shouldn't
cause trouble for your wife,

220
00:14:21,584 --> 00:14:24,794
involving her in my love life.

221
00:14:25,737 --> 00:14:29,373
But I heard that the stance
you two take toward your marriage

222
00:14:29,373 --> 00:14:31,534
is that as long as everyone's okay
with this arrangement,

223
00:14:31,534 --> 00:14:34,129
we can keep dating like this.

224
00:14:34,129 --> 00:14:37,013
But if you only focus your feelings on me,

225
00:14:37,013 --> 00:14:39,752
then this arrangement falls apart.

226
00:14:39,752 --> 00:14:41,094
And that's no good, right?

227
00:14:41,094 --> 00:14:42,729
Wait, just hold on a minute here.

228
00:14:42,729 --> 00:14:44,737
I thought this would make you happy, Chizuru.

229
00:14:44,737 --> 00:14:47,549
I suppose that's where
we have our differences.

230
00:14:47,549 --> 00:14:51,474
Because you really didn't have any idea
about what makes me happy.

231
00:14:55,521 --> 00:14:59,869
I understand the decision you made, Chizuru.

232
00:14:59,869 --> 00:15:02,009
No way!

233
00:15:02,009 --> 00:15:05,033
You've always had this slight
contempt towards me, haven't you?

234
00:15:05,033 --> 00:15:06,877
Well, that was...

235
00:15:08,273 --> 00:15:10,714
No, it's just that...

236
00:15:12,769 --> 00:15:17,617
Does this mean your criteria for romance
is not causing trouble for anyone?

237
00:15:18,273 --> 00:15:19,621
That makes sense.

238
00:15:19,621 --> 00:15:22,457
Anyway, I can live on my own.

239
00:15:22,457 --> 00:15:25,394
And I've totally given up on
the idea of having kids too.

240
00:15:26,241 --> 00:15:28,294
And since that's the case,
when it comes to romance,

241
00:15:28,294 --> 00:15:32,377
it should be fun and not something
that causes trouble for others.

242
00:15:32,377 --> 00:15:34,314
That's really what it comes down to.

243
00:15:36,065 --> 00:15:38,177
That's true.

244
00:15:39,933 --> 00:15:43,049
What about you, Sakiko?
How are things going with that guy?

245
00:15:43,049 --> 00:15:45,074
There's nothing going on between us.

246
00:15:45,689 --> 00:15:48,154
He's just a neighbor I get along well with.

247
00:15:50,637 --> 00:15:54,281
When I heard that nothing came
of that address in Nagano,

248
00:15:54,281 --> 00:15:57,474
I thought that things would
eventually just settle into place.

249
00:16:03,581 --> 00:16:07,465
I do think that he's a good person.

250
00:16:07,465 --> 00:16:09,237
I see.

251
00:16:10,381 --> 00:16:15,194
I always look forward to going to
the laundromat on Saturdays.

252
00:16:16,789 --> 00:16:20,209
I even tried not to wear the same clothes
as I did the previous week.

253
00:16:20,209 --> 00:16:23,709
I find myself being careful about doing that.

254
00:16:23,709 --> 00:16:25,469
That's good, isn't it?

255
00:16:27,049 --> 00:16:30,425
We also made a plan to go to
the home improvement store together.

256
00:16:30,425 --> 00:16:32,849
That seems very relaxed and unpretentious.

257
00:16:32,849 --> 00:16:36,705
I do enjoy being with him.

258
00:16:36,705 --> 00:16:39,114
- Well, then shouldn't you...
- However,

259
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:43,013
it feels a little different from that.

260
00:16:44,141 --> 00:16:46,773
You mean different from
how it is with Mitsuru?

261
00:16:46,773 --> 00:16:48,874
He's still in my heart.

262
00:16:49,993 --> 00:16:52,234
And unless he moves aside,

263
00:16:53,453 --> 00:16:55,674
no one else can take his place.

264
00:16:57,769 --> 00:17:00,069
Ah, yes, yes.

265
00:17:00,069 --> 00:17:02,821
See you later.
Is it okay if we say goodbye here?

266
00:17:02,821 --> 00:17:04,849
Will you be able to sleep
without having me around?

267
00:17:04,849 --> 00:17:06,653
We won't be seeing each other again
until tomorrow, you know.

268
00:17:06,653 --> 00:17:08,881
That's okay! See you tomorrow!

269
00:17:08,881 --> 00:17:10,725
Hey, what about our fist bump?

270
00:17:10,725 --> 00:17:13,954
- Hey! I'm here!
- Sho! Your bag with the cars on it!

271
00:17:23,741 --> 00:17:27,673
[Important Information
Regarding Contract Renewal]

272
00:17:52,637 --> 00:17:54,794
Long time no see.

273
00:18:00,057 --> 00:18:03,109
- It's been a year now, right?
- That's right.

274
00:18:03,109 --> 00:18:05,689
Sho's pretty amazing, being able to
go stay there overnight without crying.

275
00:18:05,689 --> 00:18:09,053
Well, I suppose Sho's the only one
who's grown at all.

276
00:18:10,205 --> 00:18:12,269
It's fine, you can go ahead
and throw that away.

277
00:18:12,269 --> 00:18:14,601
You can put it out the next day
they come to collect burnable trash.

278
00:18:14,601 --> 00:18:15,814
Is it still Mondays and Thursdays?

279
00:18:15,814 --> 00:18:18,725
But I feel like if I throw your things away,

280
00:18:18,725 --> 00:18:21,273
I might never see you again.

281
00:18:21,273 --> 00:18:23,713
- So you haven't been able to throw them away?
- No.

282
00:18:23,713 --> 00:18:26,565
Well, in that case, maybe it would
actually be better if you threw them away.

283
00:18:26,565 --> 00:18:29,301
Otherwise, you might feel as if
you were having an affair, right?

284
00:18:29,301 --> 00:18:32,813
- Huh?
- If I was always nearby,

285
00:18:32,813 --> 00:18:35,714
and always staying here, well, you know...

286
00:18:36,861 --> 00:18:41,434
By the way, tell that kid from
the coffee shop, thanks for the flowers.

287
00:18:42,549 --> 00:18:47,061
It costs money to renew, so didn't
the timing actually work out perfectly?

288
00:18:47,061 --> 00:18:49,541
Good luck with getting things
back to their original state.

289
00:18:49,541 --> 00:18:53,605
Also, I think you might be
spoiling Sho a little too much.

290
00:18:53,605 --> 00:18:56,297
You mustn't be afraid that he'll dislike you.
Just raise him properly!

291
00:18:56,297 --> 00:18:57,885
Azusa.

292
00:18:57,885 --> 00:19:00,377
I really am grateful to Miki.

293
00:19:00,377 --> 00:19:02,894
I was happy to be able to
gain a sibling when we married.

294
00:19:02,894 --> 00:19:04,981
It's fine. Why not just be here?

295
00:19:04,981 --> 00:19:07,653
Oh, and I really don't like my mother-in-law.

296
00:19:07,653 --> 00:19:09,821
I dislike her so much that
I've even come to dislike Ibaraki itself.

297
00:19:09,821 --> 00:19:12,373
- Even though I'm dead, I still dislike her.
- Azusa!

298
00:19:12,373 --> 00:19:15,394
But I put up with it
because I love you, Itsuki.

299
00:19:16,285 --> 00:19:21,893
She may be a nasty old hag,
but she did still give birth to you.

300
00:19:21,893 --> 00:19:23,353
- So I was even able to force a smile.
- Why, even now...

301
00:19:23,353 --> 00:19:26,354
- I really was amazing when I was alive.
- am I still seeing Azusa?

302
00:19:27,313 --> 00:19:30,065
Well, I suppose a bit of a push
in the right direction is necessary.

303
00:19:30,065 --> 00:19:32,994
- When you're transferring...
- Why did you have to die?

304
00:19:34,961 --> 00:19:37,834
I wanted to spend my life with you, Azusa.

305
00:19:41,185 --> 00:19:43,154
Yes, that's true.

306
00:19:43,841 --> 00:19:45,593
But it can't be helped, right?

307
00:19:46,225 --> 00:19:48,794
I'm not around anymore,
so you can't make that choice.

308
00:19:55,141 --> 00:19:56,945
Azusa.

309
00:19:57,881 --> 00:20:00,554
My wording might be slightly off here, but...

310
00:20:02,581 --> 00:20:04,314
Take care.

311
00:20:24,633 --> 00:20:26,513
[Itsuki Sonoda -
Are you almost done with work?]

312
00:20:26,513 --> 00:20:29,693
[I'm making Napolitan spaghetti.
Would you like to come over and have some?]

313
00:20:34,585 --> 00:20:37,361
- Thanks for the food.
- Thanks for the food.

314
00:20:41,109 --> 00:20:44,153
Wow, this is delicious! Incredible!

315
00:20:44,765 --> 00:20:47,229
No, actually it's Cookpad
who deserves the credit for this.

316
00:20:47,229 --> 00:20:49,245
After trying to make it for about a year,
I guess it's finally edible now...

317
00:20:49,245 --> 00:20:50,929
No, it's really good.

318
00:20:50,929 --> 00:20:52,581
- You really put a lot of effort into this.
- It's nothing.

319
00:20:52,581 --> 00:20:54,861
Oh right, I also bought some
powdered parmesan cheese.

320
00:21:00,937 --> 00:21:02,797
Here you go.

321
00:21:05,165 --> 00:21:08,933
The contract for this place
will be up for renewal in another two months.

322
00:21:08,933 --> 00:21:11,509
The timing is pretty good,
so I've also been thinking of moving.

323
00:21:11,509 --> 00:21:13,037
Oh, that's right.

324
00:21:13,037 --> 00:21:15,097
I'll help you with your move.

325
00:21:16,193 --> 00:21:18,585
What about you, Mrs. Seo?

326
00:21:18,585 --> 00:21:21,733
Well, I do wonder about living
all by myself in a house like that.

327
00:21:24,353 --> 00:21:26,069
This is delicious.

328
00:21:26,921 --> 00:21:29,373
Because he might come back?

329
00:21:32,433 --> 00:21:35,853
Do you plan to keep living there by yourself?

330
00:21:36,873 --> 00:21:39,853
Well, I don't have any plans
to move for the time being.

331
00:21:39,853 --> 00:21:42,933
I'm going to ask a question that might be
so brazen as to be almost off-putting.

332
00:21:42,933 --> 00:21:45,941
It's okay if you want to back out of this,
but please just hear me out for a minute.

333
00:21:45,941 --> 00:21:48,573
Are you sure it would be backing out?

334
00:21:48,573 --> 00:21:50,901
What is it?

335
00:21:50,901 --> 00:21:52,393
I'm opening the parmesan cheese.

336
00:21:52,393 --> 00:21:57,293
Would it be an option for me and Sho
to move in with you, Mrs. Seo?

337
00:22:02,473 --> 00:22:03,593
Huh?

338
00:22:03,593 --> 00:22:06,253
Would it be an option
for the three of us to live together?

339
00:22:09,681 --> 00:22:11,589
No, that's not an option.

340
00:22:13,041 --> 00:22:16,649
I see. Understood.

341
00:22:19,205 --> 00:22:22,701
If we move, it should happen
before Sho starts school, right?

342
00:22:22,701 --> 00:22:27,113
Children are more sensitive to changes
in their environment than adults are.

343
00:22:27,113 --> 00:22:28,853
Yes, that's true.

344
00:22:29,673 --> 00:22:33,013
I wonder what kind of layout would be best
for a parent and child living together?

345
00:22:35,341 --> 00:22:38,005
Sunlight is also important too, right?

346
00:22:38,005 --> 00:22:39,975
But since we'll be moving anyway,

347
00:22:39,975 --> 00:22:42,981
maybe I'll just go ahead
and buy a drum-style dryer.

348
00:22:42,981 --> 00:22:46,021
- You have a drum-style one, right?
- Hold on a minute.

349
00:22:46,021 --> 00:22:48,993
- Yes?
- I can't just let this slide.

350
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:51,813
- What?
- What do you mean, "what"?

351
00:22:52,477 --> 00:22:54,133
Why does it feel like
we've ended up living together?

352
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:55,509
No, it's fine if that's not an option.

353
00:22:55,509 --> 00:22:57,481
- I just thought that it might be, that's all.
- Why did you think that?

354
00:22:57,481 --> 00:22:59,433
Because I'm lonely.

355
00:23:03,973 --> 00:23:06,105
Mr. Sonoda.

356
00:23:06,105 --> 00:23:08,901
The thought of wanting to live with someone
just because of loneliness...

357
00:23:08,901 --> 00:23:11,241
You aren't the sort of person
who would think about things so simply, right?

358
00:23:11,241 --> 00:23:14,933
That's right. It's not like
I'd want to live with just anyone.

359
00:23:19,993 --> 00:23:22,757
Oh, sorry. Let me take care of that. Sorry.

360
00:23:32,073 --> 00:23:36,453
I suppose I am also lonely.

361
00:23:38,537 --> 00:23:40,413
But I'm sorry.

362
00:23:41,229 --> 00:23:43,213
Something like that,

363
00:23:43,969 --> 00:23:46,653
I still can't think about it right now.

364
00:23:48,629 --> 00:23:50,369
I'm sorry.

365
00:23:53,117 --> 00:23:57,053
Soon it will be one year since the accident.

366
00:23:58,061 --> 00:24:01,093
Do you think you could
give me an answer after that?

367
00:24:03,125 --> 00:24:04,845
Huh?

368
00:24:04,845 --> 00:24:09,385
I believe I just refused.

369
00:24:09,385 --> 00:24:11,333
Please think it over.

370
00:24:18,997 --> 00:24:21,533
When shall we go to
the home improvement store?

371
00:24:23,993 --> 00:24:26,453
All right, I'll think it over.

372
00:24:52,128 --> 00:24:53,128
[Café Hikouki]

373
00:24:53,128 --> 00:24:55,773
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you.

374
00:24:59,849 --> 00:25:01,293
What happened today?

375
00:25:01,293 --> 00:25:02,805
Huh?

376
00:25:02,805 --> 00:25:05,953
It's not often that
you ask someone for help, Naoto.

377
00:25:05,953 --> 00:25:08,648
But it's not like it's especially crowded,

378
00:25:08,648 --> 00:25:10,573
so I was wondering
if maybe something happened.

379
00:25:14,989 --> 00:25:16,791
No, don't worry about it, it's totally fine.

380
00:25:16,791 --> 00:25:18,693
I didn't have anything else going on anyway.

381
00:25:20,449 --> 00:25:23,037
Okay, I'll be taking care of
some administrative work,

382
00:25:23,037 --> 00:25:25,745
- so would it be okay if you do the cleaning?
- Sure, no problem.

383
00:25:25,745 --> 00:25:29,133
- Also, the phone...
- Huh?

384
00:25:29,757 --> 00:25:31,673
Could you answer it?

385
00:25:32,549 --> 00:25:34,373
I mean, if anyone calls?

386
00:25:37,069 --> 00:25:40,133
Okay, sure.

387
00:26:36,341 --> 00:26:38,853
Hello, this is Café Hikouki.

388
00:26:48,001 --> 00:26:49,721
<i>Sakiko?</i>

389
00:26:56,041 --> 00:26:58,839
Yes. Mitsuru?

390
00:27:00,706 --> 00:27:02,479
It's been a while.

391
00:27:04,137 --> 00:27:07,399
<i>Yes. Are you doing well?</i>

392
00:27:08,505 --> 00:27:10,365
I'm fine.

393
00:27:11,165 --> 00:27:12,989
How about you?

394
00:27:13,657 --> 00:27:16,039
<i>I'm fine.</i>

395
00:27:17,859 --> 00:27:21,799
It's been pretty hot out, but are you okay?
Are you eating well?

396
00:27:22,853 --> 00:27:26,279
<i>I am. How about you, Sakiko?</i>

397
00:27:27,421 --> 00:27:30,359
Yes. I'm eating well.

398
00:27:32,229 --> 00:27:34,039
Are you sleeping well too?

399
00:27:35,345 --> 00:27:37,341
<i>I am.</i>

400
00:27:39,973 --> 00:27:44,889
Listen, I heard that it's possible
to get heatstroke even while sleeping.

401
00:27:44,889 --> 00:27:47,999
So make sure to drink a full glass of water
before you go to sleep.

402
00:27:49,633 --> 00:27:51,405
<i>I see.</i>

403
00:27:53,633 --> 00:27:55,439
And as for the shop,

404
00:27:56,205 --> 00:27:59,797
all the regular customers
are still coming as usual.

405
00:27:59,797 --> 00:28:02,293
So I think things are going well,

406
00:28:02,293 --> 00:28:04,397
though I was a bit worried at first.

407
00:28:04,397 --> 00:28:07,681
Naoto's doing a very good job by himself.

408
00:28:07,681 --> 00:28:10,601
And I also stop by to help out on occasion.

409
00:28:10,601 --> 00:28:14,869
- <i>Aren't you asking me where I am...</i>
- The coffee that Naoto brews

410
00:28:15,765 --> 00:28:17,117
has gotten really good.

411
00:28:17,117 --> 00:28:18,733
<i>Or why I disappeared?</i>

412
00:28:18,733 --> 00:28:21,799
It's now just about
as good as your coffee, Mitsuru.

413
00:28:23,017 --> 00:28:24,687
It's just...

414
00:28:25,768 --> 00:28:27,424
about the same.

415
00:28:29,301 --> 00:28:31,039
About the same.

416
00:28:33,221 --> 00:28:34,906
<i>Why aren't you...</i>

417
00:28:36,017 --> 00:28:37,674
<i>asking me?</i>

418
00:28:46,445 --> 00:28:48,449
Don't lie to me.

419
00:28:48,449 --> 00:28:52,743
But if there's something
you don't want to talk about,

420
00:28:52,743 --> 00:28:54,474
then you don't have to tell me.

421
00:28:56,205 --> 00:28:59,279
<i>I decided, you know, when we got married.</i>

422
00:29:00,145 --> 00:29:01,977
<i>That brings back memories.</i>

423
00:29:04,085 --> 00:29:06,319
If you won't tell me, Mitsuru,

424
00:29:07,345 --> 00:29:09,239
or if you don't want to tell me,
then that's okay.

425
00:29:11,097 --> 00:29:13,359
I mean, if you wanted
to tell me, you would, right?

426
00:29:14,117 --> 00:29:16,479
It's okay not to tell me anything
you'd rather not talk about.

427
00:29:17,893 --> 00:29:19,959
Because we're still husband and wife.

428
00:29:23,901 --> 00:29:27,039
Maybe that's just what
our family registry says,

429
00:29:28,357 --> 00:29:30,221
but we're still husband and wife.

430
00:29:31,545 --> 00:29:33,289
<i>Yes.</i>

431
00:29:36,937 --> 00:29:38,797
But...

432
00:29:38,797 --> 00:29:40,937
<i>Yes?</i>

433
00:29:40,937 --> 00:29:43,233
But I'm sorry.

434
00:29:43,233 --> 00:29:45,519
There is just one thing I want to ask you.

435
00:29:48,477 --> 00:29:51,599
Because some things aren't just issues
between husbands and wives.

436
00:29:53,013 --> 00:29:54,753
<i>Yes.</i>

437
00:29:57,097 --> 00:29:58,999
Azusa Sonoda.

438
00:30:01,161 --> 00:30:02,999
Why did you take her with you?

439
00:30:09,121 --> 00:30:11,879
Sorry, but I had a look at your phone.

440
00:30:13,145 --> 00:30:16,939
And I went to the address in Nagano
that was written down in your notes.

441
00:30:16,939 --> 00:30:17,965
I didn't know the person who lived there,

442
00:30:17,965 --> 00:30:19,472
and they didn't know anything
about you or Azusa.

443
00:30:19,472 --> 00:30:21,193
That's what they said.

444
00:30:21,193 --> 00:30:23,609
They didn't know anything.

445
00:30:23,609 --> 00:30:25,881
But

446
00:30:25,881 --> 00:30:28,159
since you'd written down
that address in your notes,

447
00:30:29,345 --> 00:30:31,799
that was a place you wanted to go, right?

448
00:30:39,101 --> 00:30:42,017
Well, whatever. It's fine.

449
00:30:42,017 --> 00:30:46,239
You can go wherever you want,
and do whatever you want.

450
00:30:47,373 --> 00:30:49,205
That's fine, but...

451
00:30:51,661 --> 00:30:54,359
Why did you go together with Azusa?

452
00:30:55,357 --> 00:30:57,293
You know, right?

453
00:30:57,293 --> 00:31:01,079
There was an accident, and she died.
You know that, right?

454
00:31:01,917 --> 00:31:04,479
Why did you go together with Azusa?

455
00:31:05,133 --> 00:31:07,205
That...

456
00:31:07,205 --> 00:31:09,399
If I don't know that,

457
00:31:10,541 --> 00:31:11,723
there are people who will keep suffering

458
00:31:11,723 --> 00:31:14,159
if they don't know what happened, understand?

459
00:31:15,105 --> 00:31:17,865
There are people who haven't been able to
get answers to that this whole time,

460
00:31:17,865 --> 00:31:20,839
and so they have to keep thinking about it.

461
00:31:27,135 --> 00:31:31,833
The two of you went out together
without telling any of us,

462
00:31:31,833 --> 00:31:35,759
I can pretty much guess
what kind of relationship you had,

463
00:31:39,433 --> 00:31:41,599
but I want you to explain.

464
00:31:45,301 --> 00:31:49,513
And please think of Mr. Sonoda too.
You know, right?

465
00:31:49,513 --> 00:31:50,818
He has a kid too.

466
00:31:50,818 --> 00:31:54,041
A 6-year-old boy who will be starting
elementary school next year.

467
00:31:54,041 --> 00:31:55,649
Azusa left behind that kid,

468
00:31:55,649 --> 00:31:59,879
she was a beloved wife,
and she died because of you.

469
00:32:01,937 --> 00:32:03,665
<i>Yes.</i>

470
00:32:07,539 --> 00:32:09,479
Why were you together?

471
00:32:19,105 --> 00:32:22,599
Whatever, it's fine.

472
00:32:24,453 --> 00:32:26,273
I understand.

473
00:32:29,185 --> 00:32:32,599
That's what we decided, right?
You don't have to tell me.

474
00:32:34,901 --> 00:32:36,653
Sorry.

475
00:32:38,549 --> 00:32:40,397
Sorry to ask you that.

476
00:32:47,233 --> 00:32:49,017
<i>Sakiko.</i>

477
00:32:51,241 --> 00:32:53,049
What?

478
00:32:54,561 --> 00:32:56,559
<i>I'm glad you sound well.</i>

479
00:32:58,233 --> 00:33:00,079
<i>Take care.</i>

480
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:08,841
I will.

481
00:33:10,221 --> 00:33:12,639
You take care too, Mitsuru.

482
00:33:31,197 --> 00:33:32,919
I'm sorry.

483
00:33:33,697 --> 00:33:37,559
There were some things I knew,
but I kept them hidden.

484
00:33:41,373 --> 00:33:43,119
I mean, I...

485
00:33:44,761 --> 00:33:47,817
I've been on Mr. Sonoda's side
this whole time, haven't I?

486
00:33:47,817 --> 00:33:50,359
I was surprised by the things I was saying.

487
00:33:51,897 --> 00:33:53,645
Yes.

488
00:33:55,539 --> 00:33:57,479
I'm going home now.

489
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:06,761
<i>I'd been thinking, the next time
I got a call from Mitsuru,</i>

490
00:34:06,761 --> 00:34:09,969
<i>I'd ask him what I did wrong,</i>

491
00:34:09,969 --> 00:34:12,799
<i>and what it would take for us
to go back to being husband and wife.</i>

492
00:34:13,509 --> 00:34:16,919
<i>I'd planned to ask him that calmly.</i>

493
00:34:24,577 --> 00:34:26,919
<i>But instead, the things that I said</i>

494
00:34:28,857 --> 00:34:31,319
<i>were all said with someone else in mind.</i>

495
00:34:47,801 --> 00:34:50,765
- Hello.
- Hello.

496
00:34:50,765 --> 00:34:54,159
This place is really beautiful, isn't it?

497
00:34:55,259 --> 00:35:00,477
Apparently, Azusa used to be at this church.

498
00:35:00,477 --> 00:35:03,077
That's good.

499
00:35:03,077 --> 00:35:05,679
She can be at peace and sleep well now.

500
00:35:06,865 --> 00:35:08,757
Thank you for your thoughtfulness.

501
00:35:08,757 --> 00:35:10,777
Not at all.

502
00:35:10,777 --> 00:35:14,959
Though I didn't think that
she would be coming back here like this.

503
00:35:19,641 --> 00:35:21,577
Here, Sho, look straight ahead.

504
00:35:22,817 --> 00:35:25,037
Good. And keep your back straight.

505
00:35:27,273 --> 00:35:29,289
- This one too.
- This one too.

506
00:35:29,289 --> 00:35:31,121
There are some over there too.
Shall we go take a look?

507
00:35:31,121 --> 00:35:32,213
- Okay.
- All right.

508
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:34,997
So regrettable, isn't it?

509
00:35:36,241 --> 00:35:38,439
Even though it's been a year now,

510
00:35:39,377 --> 00:35:42,377
things haven't gotten any easier.

511
00:35:55,053 --> 00:35:57,879
It's almost like being killed, isn't it?

512
00:36:00,029 --> 00:36:03,759
That's not how I see it, though.

513
00:36:05,901 --> 00:36:09,879
She had to go out with another man.

514
00:36:11,581 --> 00:36:14,959
I find it hard to believe that
Mitsuru was dragging her around.

515
00:36:16,873 --> 00:36:20,949
Maybe Azusa asked him to go along with her.

516
00:36:20,949 --> 00:36:23,959
Or maybe she asked him if it was okay
if she went along with him.

517
00:36:25,673 --> 00:36:29,199
To me, that would seem natural.

518
00:36:32,949 --> 00:36:35,399
Yes, that does sound like
something she'd say.

519
00:36:38,473 --> 00:36:40,565
Yes, it does.

520
00:36:40,565 --> 00:36:44,161
She might have said something like,
"I want to tag along".

521
00:36:44,161 --> 00:36:47,789
Yes, in that kind of vague way of speaking.

522
00:36:47,789 --> 00:36:50,985
That's exactly the sort of thing
one might say when one's mind is made up.

523
00:36:53,829 --> 00:36:57,039
Like, maybe she wanted me
to wash the bathtub.

524
00:36:58,001 --> 00:37:00,209
Is that what she said?

525
00:37:00,209 --> 00:37:01,961
Yes.

526
00:37:05,037 --> 00:37:07,279
That's very cute, isn't it?

527
00:37:09,929 --> 00:37:11,745
Yes.

528
00:37:15,385 --> 00:37:17,781
<i>As people on Azusa's side,</i>

529
00:37:17,781 --> 00:37:20,719
<i>I think it's best
if we just leave things at that.</i>

530
00:37:21,539 --> 00:37:24,559
<i>That also saves me from
resenting people more than I should.</i>

531
00:37:26,053 --> 00:37:31,359
<i>Right, being resentful is exhausting.</i>

532
00:37:33,309 --> 00:37:35,439
I don't want to be resentful.

533
00:37:42,977 --> 00:37:45,839
I like this, it feels very stable.

534
00:37:46,837 --> 00:37:48,957
Is your stepladder broken?

535
00:37:48,957 --> 00:37:50,474
No, I've never had a stepladder.

536
00:37:50,474 --> 00:37:52,721
I'd always leave high places
to Mitsuru or someone else.

537
00:37:52,721 --> 00:37:56,253
One time I tried using a chair,
and ended up falling over.

538
00:37:56,253 --> 00:37:59,679
- What?
- And since then, I've been a bit scared.

539
00:38:00,701 --> 00:38:02,769
But,

540
00:38:02,769 --> 00:38:04,100
I get the feeling that if I buy this,

541
00:38:04,100 --> 00:38:05,879
that means he's really
not coming back, you know?

542
00:38:06,917 --> 00:38:08,249
I understand.

543
00:38:08,249 --> 00:38:11,773
But it's okay now,

544
00:38:11,773 --> 00:38:13,373
so I'm going to buy it.

545
00:38:13,373 --> 00:38:15,257
All right, I can hold it for you.

546
00:38:15,257 --> 00:38:16,721
Thank you.

547
00:38:16,721 --> 00:38:18,799
- This one.
- Ah, this one, right?

548
00:38:20,353 --> 00:38:24,359
Also, I need some large trash bags.

549
00:38:41,521 --> 00:38:43,377
Oof!

550
00:38:43,377 --> 00:38:44,777
Are you all right?

551
00:38:44,777 --> 00:38:46,989
I'm fine.

552
00:38:52,421 --> 00:38:55,005
I managed to get it by myself.

553
00:38:55,005 --> 00:38:57,279
Well done.

554
00:39:04,153 --> 00:39:06,559
All right, I think I'm fine now.

555
00:39:11,073 --> 00:39:14,685
Actually, he called me again.

556
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:15,921
Huh?

557
00:39:15,921 --> 00:39:18,359
And I was able to talk to him a bit.

558
00:39:19,437 --> 00:39:22,319
Even if he did run away, I can't hate him.

559
00:39:23,801 --> 00:39:26,319
There's no way to explain it.

560
00:39:27,117 --> 00:39:29,319
I guess it's just because I love him.

561
00:39:31,029 --> 00:39:32,965
And so,

562
00:39:32,965 --> 00:39:38,289
I thought that upon hearing his voice,
I'd completely lose my heart to him.

563
00:39:40,049 --> 00:39:42,365
But actually, it was the opposite.

564
00:39:42,365 --> 00:39:44,479
Even though I was talking to Mitsuru,

565
00:39:46,085 --> 00:39:48,519
all I talked about was you, Mr. Sonoda.

566
00:39:53,501 --> 00:39:55,933
It's different with him.

567
00:39:57,153 --> 00:39:59,033
You're becoming...

568
00:40:02,797 --> 00:40:05,479
someone else who's important to me.

569
00:40:07,873 --> 00:40:10,045
During this past year,

570
00:40:10,045 --> 00:40:13,959
I've been really glad
to have you around, Mr. Sonoda.

571
00:40:15,489 --> 00:40:17,519
I was able to realize that.

572
00:40:21,009 --> 00:40:26,239
But it does just so happen to be
that you're a man and I'm a woman.

573
00:40:27,601 --> 00:40:29,679
Why are you saying it like that?

574
00:40:31,021 --> 00:40:32,897
No, it's just that

575
00:40:34,461 --> 00:40:36,589
with a man and a woman,

576
00:40:36,589 --> 00:40:38,578
what it often comes down to is,

577
00:40:38,578 --> 00:40:40,639
if that kind of relationship
is acceptable or not.

578
00:40:41,957 --> 00:40:44,685
But even if we don't have
a clearly defined relationship,

579
00:40:44,685 --> 00:40:46,759
isn't just being together
already good enough?

580
00:40:47,630 --> 00:40:49,719
As long as we feel comfortable
around each other,

581
00:40:50,517 --> 00:40:53,039
and as long as it's not
causing any trouble for anyone.

582
00:40:54,429 --> 00:41:01,376
I also don't like we have to
have a clearly defined relationship.

583
00:41:02,785 --> 00:41:07,293
Is it okay for us to just leave things
as they are, a bit ambiguous?

584
00:41:08,429 --> 00:41:11,119
Maybe I'm feeling a bit
anxious or flustered. Sorry.

585
00:41:12,425 --> 00:41:13,529
It's fine.

586
00:41:13,529 --> 00:41:16,341
And as for moving here,
no matter how I think about it...

587
00:41:16,341 --> 00:41:18,357
It would be quite sudden.

588
00:41:18,357 --> 00:41:20,617
That was quite off-putting
for you, wasn't it?

589
00:41:20,617 --> 00:41:24,177
No, but it did leave me feeling a bit shaken.

590
00:41:24,177 --> 00:41:26,993
You really scattered that parmesan cheese
everywhere, didn't you?

591
00:41:29,573 --> 00:41:32,173
I'm really sorry about that.

592
00:41:33,677 --> 00:41:36,013
I'll buy you some more.

593
00:41:46,385 --> 00:41:49,199
I'll start by getting rid of
Mitsuru's things.

594
00:41:49,801 --> 00:41:51,799
As part of sorting out my emotions.

595
00:42:06,785 --> 00:42:08,519
Alright.

596
00:42:26,149 --> 00:42:27,877
The toothbrushes as well?

597
00:42:27,877 --> 00:42:30,881
- Yes, please throw them out.
- Alright.

598
00:42:30,881 --> 00:42:33,459
By the way, are you hungry?
Shall we order some pizza?

599
00:42:33,459 --> 00:42:36,933
It doesn't have to be anything that fun.

600
00:42:36,933 --> 00:42:39,933
But eating pizza alone
leaves you feeling kind of empty.

601
00:42:39,933 --> 00:42:43,497
I don't think this can be worn either.

602
00:42:43,497 --> 00:42:45,641
Your own stuff?

603
00:42:45,641 --> 00:42:48,813
Looks like there's a lot of my stuff
to get rid of.

604
00:42:48,813 --> 00:42:50,273
You met each other

605
00:42:50,273 --> 00:42:52,773
- at a wedding ceremony, right?
- Yes.

606
00:42:52,773 --> 00:42:54,837
Oh, right.

607
00:42:54,837 --> 00:42:56,901
When we met, I was wearing this.

608
00:42:56,901 --> 00:42:58,989
Wow.

609
00:42:58,989 --> 00:43:00,465
That makes me curious.

610
00:43:00,465 --> 00:43:03,413
An encounter significant enough
to become a password.

611
00:43:03,413 --> 00:43:05,289
Password?

612
00:43:05,289 --> 00:43:08,221
Wait, today is June 28th, isn't it?

613
00:43:08,221 --> 00:43:09,269
That's right, it's today.

614
00:43:09,269 --> 00:43:12,659
Huh? Wait, really?
You're actually giving away the password?

615
00:43:12,659 --> 00:43:14,737
There wasn't anything there anyway.

616
00:43:14,737 --> 00:43:17,121
What, do you want to hear the story?

617
00:43:17,121 --> 00:43:18,505
It's a bit long.

618
00:43:18,505 --> 00:43:21,481
Sure. And besides, I think this cleaning
is going to take a while anyway.

619
00:43:21,481 --> 00:43:26,417
Okay, so it was the wedding ceremony
of one of my classmates from high school.

620
00:43:26,417 --> 00:43:27,805
Ah, the pizza's here.

621
00:43:27,805 --> 00:43:30,077
Please stay tuned for the rest of the story.

622
00:43:30,077 --> 00:43:32,719
But it's still way too early in the story.

623
00:43:35,141 --> 00:43:36,879
Coming.

624
00:43:45,917 --> 00:43:47,833
I'm home.

625
00:43:51,425 --> 00:43:53,285
Welcome back.
